  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "literal_source_and_trim",
      "evidence": "WeightedTrim:29-45,200-226; J PhysicalAtlas rows/sourceId/sourceRows_cellGuard and J TrimmedHistory definitions",
      "finding": "The source remains the union of the fourteen original ascending cells IDs0..14 except7, using their literal96-row systems and unchanged J trims. All eight coordinates and coefficient4 density remain. Union-minus-trim reconstruction requires neither a triangulation nor cell-disjointness assumption. The original constant identity constraints are not newly made strict."
    },
    {
      "id": "degenerate_affine_rows",
      "evidence": "WeightedTrim:100-218",
      "finding": "The actual rational row linear form is separated from its constant coefficient. A zero identity contributes zero and cannot witness positive slack. A nonzero constant eventually has zero majorant. A nonzero linear part has a null affine level set by the existing Haar-measure theorem. Thus no proper-row or null-wall premise is assumed. Every discarded point has one genuinely positive original row slack below width and is majorized by the finite literal row sum."
    },
    {
      "id": "real_integral_payment",
      "evidence": "WeightedTrim:41-98",
      "finding": "J point-survival and integrability imply dominated convergence of the discarded absolute sourceDensity integral. The source integral equals retained plus discarded on the same actual union. Its absolute loss is bounded by the discarded absolute integral. This does not identify any prime frontier or numerical floor integral."
    },
    {
      "id": "actual_prime_strip_payment",
      "evidence": "WeightedTrim:230-285; ActualPrimeBoxTestFunctions.tendsto_actualPrimeBoxTestSum_cube",
      "finding": "A second dominated-convergence argument pays the continuous wall majorant in the actual reciprocal-coordinate integral on cutoff..mu. For one fixed chosen majorant, the existing target-excluding prime tuple test-function theorem yields a common large-N bound. Nonnegative reciprocal-prime weights bound the actual discarded indicator mass. Arithmetic smallness is not inferred merely from pointwise geometric exhaustion and no source convergence or rejectedCost premise is introduced."
    },
    {
      "id": "signed_ordinary_bound",
      "evidence": "SignedTrimPayment:26-106,198-244,271-337",
      "finding": "The old-minus-new finite ordinary density remains signed. A two-sided compact first-cube supplier with error1 bounds both normalized densities by4/cutoff+1; the resulting absolute residual bound is8/cutoff+2. Active rows use H7<current<=R to derive valid positive residual endpoints, not current=R. P is the actual product of all eight primes and y is p7; the exact log-product dictionary supplies the quotient parameters. The reciprocal-prime mass then pays the absolute value of the signed sum."
    },
    {
      "id": "inactive_parent_and_guard",
      "evidence": "SignedTrimPayment:250-337 and CapDictionary.familyNextExponent",
      "finding": "The final actualGuardedDiscardedResidual evaluates the original CurrentParentGuard. On failure the new exponent inherits current, so the same ordinary density subtracts itself and the summand is zero. literal_source_keeps_original_current_gate proves agreement with the family selector on literal row source points. exists_actual_guarded_trim_and_integral_paid has arbitrary current functions and no CurrentParentGuard, current<=R, history, source-convergence or desired-saving caller premise. Earlier unguarded helper theorems do retain explicit genuine guard/log interfaces; they are not the final guarded claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "beta_and_common_quantifiers",
      "evidence": "SignedTrimPayment:344-429; OriginalEighthCommonBetaWidthPayment and J SignedParentLedger",
      "finding": "The production beta supplier is reused, not relabeled as new fundamental-lemma work. It keeps old-minus-new absolute rough mass in the width term with its true sign and pays the full paired error. The charge specialization uses the independent positive-w stopped continuation ledger on an even-retaining base. The final schedule fixes one n and one beta before max(Nt,Nb), before every later target, current function, cap and policy. It does not assert that this positive-w charge equals the unpresieved source integral, nor add the three separately bounded errors into a complete compiler loss."
    }
  ],
